.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt DEVD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm devd
.Nd device manager: match pci: devices and launch drivers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /sbin/devd
.Nm /sbin/devd
.Ar test
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the driver table from
.Pa /etc/drivers.toml
inside the initfs archive, reads the device directory from the
.Dq pci:
scheme, and matches each device by vendor and device id.  For a match it opens
.Pa /bar0
of the device and spawns the configured driver in a new process.  The BAR
.Dv MmioRegion
handle is transferred into the child before its first thread starts; the child
does not receive the RootDevice capability.
.Pp
The driver table is a small
.Ql [[driver]]
TOML subset:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[[driver]]
name = "dummy"
vendor = 0x1234
device = 0x11e8
exec = "/sbin/devd"
args = []
cycles = 10
.Ed
.Pp
.Va name
and
.Va exec
are required;
.Va args
defaults to an empty list and
.Va cycles
defaults to 1 with a maximum of 100.  A malformed table or an executable path
that does not start with
.Pa /
is rejected before any spawn.
.Pp
Without arguments
.Nm
launches the matched driver once and then registers the
.Dq dev:
scheme.  With
.Ar test
it launches the driver for the manifest's
.Va cycles
count, prints one
.Dq devd: driver Ar name Dq cycle N exit=C
line per cycle, reaps every child, closes every BAR handle and exits with
status 0.  This is the lifecycle path exercised by the
.Ql devd
qtest.
.Pp
The
.Ql dummy
argument is the built-in test driver.  It maps the transferred BAR, verifies
that
.Dv MMIO_CREATE
on that non-root handle fails with
.Er EPERM ,
and exits 0.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d/devd.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/drivers.toml
driver match table
.It Pa /etc/services.d/devd.toml
service manifest
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pcid 8 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr svcd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
server first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
